mission "Coalition Incident: Secret Sky"
	minor
	invisible
	to offer
		has "Coalition: First Contact: done"
		random < 3
	source "Secret Sky"
	on offer
		conversation
			`You see an Arach captain hurrying around the spaceport, speaking with anyone who will listen. He converses with each one briefly, showing something in a small monitor, and then moving on to the next shortly after. After a while, he gets to you.`
			`	"Captain? A moment if free you are?" He asks, scrambling his legs to light up the monitor. It displays a picture of a young Kimek. "A passenger of mine. Stopped by here to drop a few Saryd pilgrims, we had, but after seen them off I had, find this Kimek back in my ship, I couldn't!" He exclaims, pointing to an Arach Transport parked just before the edge of where <origin>'s dense fog cuts off your view. "Seen him anywhere, have you?"`
			choice
				`	"Sorry, I haven't. Did you try getting in touch with the local Heliarchs?"`
				`	"Sorry, but I haven't seen him either."`
					goto end
			`	He nods. "Contacted them a few hours ago, I had. Look for my passenger in the restricted sections, I wished to, but allowed there I am not, so figured that ask them for aid, I could." He sighs. "Filed a report and sent a few agents off to look for him, they did, but so far received any word from them, I have not."`
			label end
			`	He thanks you all the same for listening to him, and moves on to the next person in the spaceport to inquire about the missing Kimek.`
				decline



mission "Coalition Incident: Hunger Tower"
	minor
	invisible
	to offer
		has "Coalition: First Contact: done"
		random < 1
	source
		government "Coalition"
		attributes "kimek"
		not attributes "coalition station"
		not attributes "farming"
	on offer
		conversation
			`The spaceport here on <origin> is in something of an uproar. Thousands of Kimek are seemingly organized in what, strangely enough for a world in the Coalition, resembles a protest. Some carry devices repeatedly displaying a message in the Kimek language. Others hold signs depicting the usual Kimek diet, with their many crops sharing space with a few fish. Strangest of all, however, is how the local Heliarchs are handling the situation: they appear almost hesitant, defensively speaking to the civilians in attempts to calm them down, sometimes apologizing or simply being forced to listen to the complaints as several Kimek pile up around them.`
			`	When you finally manage to find a Heliarch who isn't occupied trying to keep the area in order, a Saryd, he explains the situation. "Missed its delivery, a food convoy has. Still investigating the issue, we are; know only that, somehow, gone missing, the entire fleet has..." He sighs, shaking his head. "Keep the locals calm we must." He goes on to help the other Heliarchs, without another word.`
			`	Within a few minutes that must've felt like hours for the stationed Heliarch agents, battalions of drones start making their way from the tallest building in the city - the hunger tower. Ferrying around several meals each, with impressive precision, the drones fly throughout the civilian mass, distributing the meals. Hundreds of larger ones head to the residential areas of the city, presumably to provide the necessary supplies for the citizens until the next food convoy arrives. Seemingly satisfied, for the moment at least, the Kimek gradually dissipate out of the spaceport and back to their homes, leaving the spaceport to the now exhausted Heliarch agents.`
				decline



mission "Coalition Incident: Arach Store"
	minor
	invisible
	to offer
		has "Coalition: First Contact: done"
		random < 2
	source
		government "Coalition"
		attributes "arach"
		not attributes "coalition station"
		not planet "Ahr"
	on offer
		conversation
			`A Heliarch patrol seems to be discussing with an Arach shop worker in front of a large, prestigious looking Arach clothing store in the spaceport. Other agents prevent you and other bystanders from approaching the scene, but you can still make out some context from their gesturing. It seems the Heliarchs are there to confiscate some pieces from the shop that you guess don't abide by their laws, while the shop worker keeps worryingly attempting to answer what questions they pose him.`
			`	Eventually, the shop owner arrives. Judging by her fine clothes, and from the reactions of the local Arachi, you figure she must either be really famous here on <origin>, or possibly belong to one of the Arach Houses, though nothing on her attire seems to indicate any specific house. She helps the worker calm down, and then she engages in conversation with the Heliarch agents as he heads back inside.`
			`	She tries to diffuse the situation, speaking calmly and attempting to take the items back into the shop, but the Heliarch agents do not budge. Running out of patience, the Heliarch in charge of the patrol cuts the Arach lady off as she's speaking, forcibly taking all the items in question, and having the agents rip apart what you guess must've been the offending parts of the cloth pieces. Stunned, the Arach simply watches as they render most of the items into unusable rags, keeping the bits they hacked away, and handing her back the other tattered remains. Without another word, they leave the scene. The Arach heads inside, and you can hear the door slam from where you're standing.`
				decline



mission "Coalition Incident: Ring of Wisdom"
	minor
	invisible
	to offer
		has "Coalition: First Contact: done"
		random < 3
	source "Ring of Wisdom"
	on offer
		conversation
			`A few minutes into your walk around the spaceport of the <origin>, the lighting suddenly shifts from the usual, comfortable tones to a cacophony of flashing warnings. Diagnostic warning messages display on all sorts of screens, and siren blasts are interrupted only by alarm messages in all three Coalition languages on repeat. You notice that not only are the civilians in the ring as alarmed as you, but every Heliarch agent you can see begins moving in a hurried, albeit organized pace, towards restricted sections, Heliarch-only rooms and warehouses.`
			`	It doesn't take long before hundreds of other Heliarchs come pouring in from other sections of the ring. When the stream finally stops, you see them take control of the machinery near the edge of the ring section, activating a huge retractable barrier that seals this section off from the rest of the ring. Ship traffic is also cut off entirely, with Heliarch squadrons keeping any ship from departing, and warships visibly walling off the hangar entrances. The Heliarchs organize the civilians swiftly, moving them away from an area where most of the agents are gathering.`
			`	As you too are herded away by the agents, you manage to get some context out of one of them - a Heliarch team that was exploring one of the ring's unknown sections had some sort of accident, and one of the members is expected to return at the area where most of the agents are gathering. The Heliarchs stand armed and ready, pointing their weapons toward a door leading to the restricted sections, and as if rendered mute by anticipation, all in the quarantined ring section appear to hold their breath, waiting.`
			`	Sure enough, the many minutes of silence are disrupted by echoing, increasingly louder screaming - one scream, incessant, coming from the shut passageway watched over by the sights of what must be a hundred Heliarch guns. A thud at the shut door briefly peaks out amidst the continuous shout. It opens to a lone, frantic Saryd, with a deeply perturbed look in his eyes. He doesn't stop at the sight of the several gun barrels pointed at him, instead drawing his own weapon, only to point it back to where he came from, firing wildly at the dark passage.`
			`	Then it stops. The screaming, and the gunshots, both stop abruptly, and the Saryd drops the gun, then collapses to the ground. He lays there, unresponsive, catatonic, as the Heliarch agents head closer to inspect him, eventually blocking him out entirely from view. A few seconds later, some of the Heliarchs back up, then bolt to a restricted room. Others stand firmly on guard, with their guns pointed either at the Saryd, or at the passageway from which he came.`
			`	Eventually, a team comes with what vaguely resembles a very large gurney, and some sort of large sack. The Heliarch agents surrounding the Saryd shuffle out of the way for those carrying the equipment to pass, and within a few minutes they're taking the Saryd away, encased in the sack as if in a body bag, carried on the gurney. Halfway to the shut down section doors, they stop as the Saryd moves erratically inside the sack, kicking and flailing wildly. It stops within a few seconds, and they resume their way out of the quarantined ring portion.`
			`	Several minutes pass before the Heliarch agents deem the passageway from where the Saryd ran from to be secure, sending some squads inside while others move to resume the ring section to normal. Once the quarantine is lifted, nearly all civilians rush to their ships, departing immediately.`
				decline
