mission "Coalition: Struggling Author 4"
	name "Kimek Publishing Company"
	description "Anna Fangvin found a Kimek publishing company who is willing to get her book published. Bring her to <destination>."
	source "Ki Patek Ka"
	destination "Inmost Blue"
	blocked "You do not have enough bunk space for Anna Fangvin and the Heliarch agent. Come back here when you have two bunks free."
	passengers 2
	to offer
		has "Coalition: Struggling Author 3: done"
	on offer
		conversation
			`The spaceport of Ki Patek Ka is vast, and would normally prove a nightmarish place to look for just one person. Thankfully, Anna being the only other human within the Coalition makes your search relatively quick. She has chosen to settle in a cafeteria with her laptop, typing away at the keyboard, presumably writing a short story to post.`
			`	"<first>! I found a company who's willing to publish me! I sent them a digital copy of my book and they instructed me to visit their office on <planet>," explains Anna, once again enthusiastic. At a table behind her you notice the figure of Temporo, speaking to a waiter.`
			choice
				`	"Great!"`
					goto go
				`	"Let's go!"`
					goto go
				`	"What's the publishing company called?"`
			`	"They're called 'Priyepichia Publishing.'" Anna shows you beautiful pictures of a clean white building perched on a mountainside, high above gentle waves. On the roof stands a landing pad painted with a striped, sleek beetle-like creature whose hind legs resemble broad paddles.`
			label go
			`	You head back to your ship with Anna and Temporo, and plot a course to <destination>.`
				accept
	on complete
		event "beyond the hyperdrive is published" 165 197
		conversation
			`Landing on <planet>, Anna is excitedly holding a copy of 'Beyond the Hyperdrive.' She hastily opens the hatch as soon as it unlocks.`
			`	Anna stops, waiting for you to catch up. "In the message they sent me, they included instructions on how to reach their offices," she explains. "Let's go!"`
			`	Several long streets later, Anna is completely lost. "This isn't where the instructions were supposed to lead at all," she says, turning to Temporo, who has been following you the whole time. "Do you know how to get there?"`
			`	The Heliarch takes the lead, and within minutes you reach a train station. Once the train arrives, you travel to a neighborhood where a large white building dominates the skyline.`
			`	Circling around to the publisher's office, you find the entrance bustling with Kimek, along with the occasional Saryd and Arach coming and going. Anna looks for a front desk and directs you to a Kimek who appears to be a receptionist.`
			choice
				`	"Hello, do you happen to know where Priyepichia Publishing is?"`
				`	"We're looking for a publishing company called Priyepichia Publishing. Could you provide directions?"`
			`	"On the 16th floor, Priyepichia Publishing is. Over there, the elevators are," says the receptionist's translator.`
			`	You turn to where the Kimek points you and see six large elevators, larger than what you are familiar with in human space. Temporo leads you to the least crowded one.`
			`	The three of you enter the elevator. It makes stops at each floor of the building, and the elevator gets quieter as more Kimek reach their destinations. When you reach the 16th floor, the elevator is only half full. The door opens to reveal a Kimek, wearing an ornate jeweled necklace as well as a translation device.`
			choice
				`	"Hello?"`
				`	(Exit the elevator.)`
			`	"Greetings, humans. Follow me, you must, so discuss your book, we can," the Kimek says through its translation box.`
			`	At the direction of the Kimek, you and Anna walk as directed until you arrive at a room with glass walls. Along the way, you pass a lounge, a conference area where multiple Kimek are discussing something at a table with a group of Heliarchs, and a large open workspace where individual Kimek sit at their own computers.`
			`	After a few minutes of walking, you reach an office where another Kimek sits with a team of Heliarchs. Temporo takes a seat with them, making six - two from each species.`
			`	The Kimek guiding you gestures toward the office and heads over to speak with the group.`
			`	As you enter, Anna puts down the copy of her book on the table, and you each take a seat. The Kimek that led you here briefly speaks to the other non-Heliarch Kimek sitting at the interview table before leaving.`
			`	The sitting Kimek's translation device begins speaking.`
			`	"Greetings. Ikiyachee, my name is, and head editor of Priyepichia Publishing, I am. To see an alien want to publish a book, interesting and unexpected it was," the Kimek says.`
			`	"Hello, I am Anna Fangvin, and this is my friend <first> <last>, who has been very helpful in bringing me here," Anna says, somewhat flustered.`
			`	"From the introduction and the first few pages, interesting your book sounded, but run it past the Heliarch reviewers, we must. So, <first>, long and intensive, this interview will be. As very unique, to meet a human like her is, and to adapt her book to our culture, a long and drawn-out process it will be."`
			choice
				`	"How long will I have to wait?"`
				`	"Should I stay here to accompany Anna?`
					goto accompany
			label "wait time"
			`	"Wait a few hours during our preliminary interview, you must.`
			choice
				`	"A few hours? That's quite boring, isn't it?"`
				`	"Should I stay here to accompany Anna?"`
					goto accompany
			label boring
			`	"If boring for you, the interview is, then leave you may, to the lounge."`
			choice
				`	"Then I'm going to the lounge. Where is it?"`
				`	(Accompany Anna during the interview.)`
					goto "stay in interview"
			label "directions to lounge"
			`	Ikiyachee gives you directions to the lounge, and you head there to wait out the interview.`
				goto lounge
			label "accompany"
			`	"To stay with her during the interview, we allow you to, but a lounge for you, we have. If too boring, the interview is, then leave you may."`
			choice
				`	(Wait in the lounge.)`
					goto "directions to lounge"
				`	(Accompany Anna during the interview.)`
			label "stay in interview"
			`	Once the first questions are asked, Anna is all too happy to begin discussing the contents of her novel in great detail.`
			`	Under the watchful eye of the six Heliarchs in the room, Anna explains her anti-Quarg sentiments, the reasoning behind her choice to write the book, and the content of the book. She speaks quickly, but the Heliarchs' numerous questions for clarification and elaboration make the process a long one.`
			`	"Sold many books before coming here, have you?" Temporo asks. Anna embarrassedly glances in your direction. "Well, no," she replies. "But I've been writing better and better over the past few years."`
			`	Priyepichia's representative speaks up. "Word count, we must know. Binding process, aware of you are? What type and cover style, want you?"`
			`	"The hardcover book should have a jump drive emblazoned on the front cover. I'm not sure the exact options for a binding type in this area of space; couldn't you just decide that yourself?"`
			`	As you listen, you learn that due to the Coalition's review process to make the book more suitable, Anna will have to stay for about half a year, during which she will have an apartment to live in.`
